    "note": "WS-8 (2026-08-30): CKM_AES_XTS (and CKM_AES_XTS_KEY_GEN) did not exist in this engine at all before this session -- required a new CKK_AES_XTS key type (32/64-byte double-length raw key), threaded through the object model everywhere CKK_AES was hardcoded (P11Attributes.cpp check-value computation x2, SoftHSM_objects.cpp object-factory dispatch, OSSLAES.cpp getCipher, whose AES bit-length gate hardcoded 128/192/256). Deliberately routed check-value computation and key generation through the same generic SHA-256(keyBits)-based path already used for CKK_CHACHA20/HMAC key types (not AESKey::getKeyCheckValue, which internally assumes 128/192/256-bit keys) -- avoids a second, parallel double-length-key problem in the check-value code path. Cases picked for real ciphertext stealing (payloadLen deliberately NOT a multiple of 16 bytes, so a plain block-cipher pass could not silently accept the wrong output length): verified via a standalone C program (xts_test.c) that a single EVP_EncryptUpdate call handles the ciphertext-stealing correctly, before touching the C++. Restricted to tweakMode=hex test groups -- this engine takes the Data Unit Sequence Number as a raw 16-byte value per PKCS#11 v3.2 section 6.15.4, matching hex mode directly; number mode (deriving the tweak from a sequence-number counter) is a distinct ACVP test convention this mechanism does not need to implement."
